 baseline, rebooted node1, confirmed the boot ID changed, and verified the inventory app, SELinux enforcing mode, and the port label all recovered post-restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1: confirmed SELinux Enforcing, no existing inventory app, no web server installed\",\"Installed httpd and policycoreutils-python-utils\",\"Created inventory application content at /var/www/html/index.html and restored SELinux context\",\"Added /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory-port.conf with 'Listen 8181'\",\"Diagnosed httpd bind failure as SELinux permission denial (port 8181 was labeled intermapper_port_t)\",\"Reassigned port 8181 to http_port_t via 'semanage port -m -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181'\",\"Enabled and started httpd; verified curl access on $NODE_IP:8181 and SELinux still Enforcing with no AVC denials\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, SELinux mode, httpd status, app response, port label)\",\"Triggered a background systemd reboot on node1 so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned\",\"Verified changed boot_id and confirmed post-restart recovery: SELinux Enforcing, httpd active, port 8181 listening and labeled http_port_t, inventory app serving content, no AVC denials\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app served on TCP 8181 with SELinux enforcing (functional requirement)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3e2f9604bee44937\"],\"summary\":\"httpd active, port 8181 listening, curl returns inventory HTML, getenforce=Enforcing, no AVC denials\"},{\"requirement\":\"SELinux MAC root cause diagnosis and fix\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6aea5476382c4c89\",\"cmd-3e2f9604bee44937\"],\"summary\":\"journalctl showed 'Permission denied' binding 8181 (SELinux, since apachectl configtest passed); confirmed port 8181 was labeled intermapper_port_t, not http_port_t; fixed via semanage port -m and re-verified successful bind\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 pre-restart healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-19e8f92c31c